{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1304470-timeline-of-the-scion-ks-printing","id":1304470,"title":"Timeline of the Scion KS Printing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-12T11:24:23-07:00","id":1304470,"title":"Timeline of the Scion KS Printing","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> This is a timeline of events in the last 8 months in creation and publication of Scion 2nd Edition. The dates listed were taken from Kickstarter Updates, Monday Meeting Progress Notes, Onyx Path forums (specifically the errata collection dates), and my DriveThru library entries.<br /> <br /> At first blush, one might assume this is a passive aggressive comment on delays experienced in the Scion 2nd Edition project. That\u2019s not accurate, but I can see where one might make that assumption. I\u2019ve been fine with the time required to get the game in the best shape possible. I did put this together however, because of the lost errata situation. If you\u2019re unfamiliar with it, Rich Thomas provides an overview in the Monday Meeting notes from April 8th, 2019. <br /> <br /> Rich has said he\u2019ll share what he knows once he has some definitive information, and I have faith he will. Doing my own due diligence as a Kickstarter backer, I started following one of his long standing recommendations and \u201cread the Progress Notes.\u201d In addition, I started reading community questions and the direct communications from Onyx Path staff in the Monday Meeting comments.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not difficult to get confused. Not because the information or the notes are confusing in of themselves, but I\u2019m looking at roughly 8 months. There are a lot of common terms that mean different things depending on the context. For example terms like proof and print can be nouns, verbs, and apply to entirely different separate stages in this whole big process. The term \u201cfiles\u201d can pertain to the Prestige print run, the POD print run, the Advance Backer PDF, or the Post-errata PDF. Add to that, these events all run and bleed into each other over months in weekly installments. <br /> <br /> So I broke it into a timeline. That way when Rich does have some information he can share, I can put it context. Or a continuum if you like. And I\u2019m sharing it with the community. I DO NOT want to foist any conclusions on anyone. This post is not an allegation or an indictment. Do I have questions? Definitely and hopefully this will help me (and you) ask BETTER questions. The community will draw it\u2019s own conclusions as is proper.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I strived to only provide accurate information. I DO interpret what I think the Progress Notes are meant to communicate, but I did so in good faith. If I have gotten anything wrong, I welcome correction from an informed source. I\u2019m not trying to mislead anyone.<br /> <br /> <u>Let me offer a few common definitions for clarity. It helps to be specific:</u><br /> <b>Prestige hardcover</b>: The book store quality version of the book that backers will receive from pledging for a hard copy in the Kickstarter. It went through a separate proofing process than the POD version. If it\u2019s not POD, it\u2019s Prestige.<br /> <br /> <b>POD or POD hard copy</b>: Either the digital file used for a Print-on-Demand hard copy or an physical book created on spec by DriveThru. The release of final backer PDF has been tied directly to this digital file. If it\u2019s not Prestige, it\u2019s POD.<br /> <br /> <b>Advance PDF</b>: A PDF shared with the community that is not expected to perfect or final. They\u2019re both previews to backers and a tool for the community to help identify errata.<br /> <br /> <b>Post-errata PDF</b>: This is either the finished PDF with all the corrections (that backers are waiting on, as of this writing), or\u2026 it\u2019s the PDF released after April 2nd which was intended to final.<br /> <br /> <br /> Without further ado.<br /> <br /> <b>July 9th, 2018</b> The <b>Origin</b> Advance PDF is made available to Backers. This was Pre-Errata and not expected to be finished or final, and may have had missing art. That said, it had a preliminary layout.<br /> <br /> <b>July 10th to August 19th, 2018</b> This is the period open for backers to assist with errata collection for <b>Origin</b>. The thread is locked on the 19th.<br /> <br /> <b>October 17th, 2018</b> The <b>Hero</b> Advance PDF is made available to Backers. This was Pre-Errata and not expected to be finished or final, and may have had missing art. That said, it had a preliminary layout.<br /> <br /> <b>October 18th to November 11th, 2018</b> This is the period open for backers to assist with errata collection for <b>Hero</b>. The thread is locked on the 11th.<br /> <br /> <b>February 11th, 2019</b> The Monday Meeting notes reflect that <b>Origin</b> and <b>Hero</b> have the following status \u2013 <i>Putting printer files together, sending to press this week.</i> This refers to the Prestige Hard Cover. Spelling it out a little more, this is when Onyx Path was preparing their digital file to be sent to sent to the Prestige printer, so that printer can create and return a prestige proof copy.<br /> <br /> <b>February 18th, 2019</b> The status or <b>Origin</b> and <b>Hero</b> changes to <i>At the printer.</i> What this is telling us is that the Prestige Printer has Onyx Path\u2019s digital file and is creating a proof of the Prestige hard copy, which will be returned to Onyx Path for them to inspect.<br /> <br /> <b>February 25th, 2019</b> The status of <b>Origin</b> and <b>Hero</b> upgraded to <i>Getting printer proofs this week.</i> At this point, Onyx Path was expecting the Prestige printer proof to arrive.<br /> <br /> <b>March 4th, 2019</b> The status of <b>Origin</b> and <b>Hero</b> upgraded to <i>Printer proofs returned. BackerKit site orders getting locked Weds.</i> This means that the prestige printer proof was reviewed and sent back to the prestige printer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>March 11th, 2019</b> The status of <b>Origin</b> and <b>Hero</b> changes to <i>\u201dPrinting. PoD proof ordered.\u201d</i> This update communicates two different things on one bullet point. First, an actual print order for the Prestige hard covers has been issued or released. Secondly, Onyx Path sent DriveThru a digital file, so that DriveThru can produce a POD proof for Onyx Path to examine.<br /> <br /> Again, for emphasis, this the point at which the Prestige had copies were released to print.<br /> <br /> <b>My only comment</b>: At this point, backers begin to ask weekly for a post-errata PDF, because they\u2019re reading that the Prestige hard covers have been released for fabrication. The response every week is that the post-errata PDF is being held until the Proof copy from DriveThru has been received, examined, and approved. Pointing this out might constitute an editorial on my part, but it\u2019s also what happened.<br /> <br /> <b>March 18th, 2019</b> The status of <b>Origin</b> and <b>Hero</b> remain at <i>\u201dPrinting. PoD proof ordered.\u201d</i> Same as the previous update, we can assume they\u2019re waiting to receive the POD proof from DriveThru to arrive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b> March 25th, 2019</b> the status of <b>Origin</b> and <b>Hero</b> are changed to <i> Printing wrapping up this week.</i> I believe this status on applies to the Prestige hard copy printing and that DriveThru\u2019s POD proof is still ongoing.<br /> <br /> <b>April 1st, 2019</b> the status of <b>Origin</b> and <b>Hero</b> change to <i>\u201dShipping from printer to fulfillment shipper this week.\u201d</i> This pertains to the Prestige hardcopies, but Rich addresses the POD in comment I\u2019ll quote below.<br /> <br /> To put a capstone on this timeline, this is a quote by Rich from the April 1st Monday Meeting comments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rich Thomas on April 2nd</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I haven\u2019t notified backers in an Update yet, as I need to also set up the PoD coupons, but the final PDFs are already up today. You can download the updated ones in your DTRPG library. If you\u2019re not a backer, Scion will be available to the public on DTRPG around the same time as stores will have the physical books.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>April 2nd, 2019</b> There\u2019s no status update on this date, but <i>what Onyx Path believed</i> to be the Post-Errata PDF (otherwise known as the \u201cFinal PDF\u201d) was updated on DriveThru. This is the first opportunity that backers to see what they expect to be the full and corrected rule set.<br /> <br /> <b>During the next week</b> Backers discover that not all the errata appears in the \u201cFinal PDF.\u201d Neall Price becomes aware of the situation as so does Onyx Path salaried staff. Neall begins to the review the \u201cFinal PDF\u201d in detail to determine what made it into the file and what didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> <b>April 8th, 2019</b> The status of <b>Origin</b> and <b>Hero</b> is <i>Shipping from printer to fulfillment shipper this week.</i> In the body of that day\u2019s blog entry, Rich made a more detailed report explaining the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rich Thomas on April 8th, 2019[/quote</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today, though, we were less happy with having to get together during the meeting and talk about how we need to figure out what broke in our proofing process with our Scion 2e core books.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll talk more about this when we get all the information in, but it seems pretty sure that a number of errata fixes that Neall input did not \u201cstick\u201d, but remained as errors. He is currently, painstakingly, going back through his errata notes and reconstructing what changes need to be made.<br /> <br /> The last I checked, he hasn\u2019t found a pattern for why some changes stayed, and others did not, nor why this happened with these two books, but not on the dozen-plus books that have previously used the same proofing process. While I\u2019d like to know that, and will, our in-house devs have already taken over the errata input phase so that our book developers only have to notate the PDF.<br /> <br /> This will add another stage, but will also give us an additional chance to identify whether errata that we gathered is actually in a book.<br /> We\u2019ll be able to tell better once Neall finishes his pass, but we\u2019re not seeing anything that breaks the game or makes it unplayable. Certainly, the rules as they stand have worked for the many Scion 2e groups who are already playing the game, including the fraction of Actual Play groups we can highlight each week in our Media section below.<br /> <br /> But it is extremely frustrating for us, and Neall, but also for all of the Scion community that stepped up to pore through the Backer PDF and send us what they found. Sometimes, in publishing, despite all your safeguards, stuff slips in. Here\u2019s a painful example of a process that worked\u2026until it didn\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rich followed up after a question in the comments with the following statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rich Thomas, April 8th, 2019</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Folks, just to put this upfront: if I intended right now to go into details of what may or may not have been affected by the errata problem, or details of our proofing process, beyond what I\u2019ve written about here or in previous MMN blogs, I would have gone into those details already. Not trying to be cute, we really do need to determine the extent of the issue before we can solve any problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1789,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","user":"Quinarch","date":".  Bringing the timeline forward to April 13th 04-13-2019, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T23:50:56-07:00","id":1304585,"title":"","content":"Thanks for this. Do you have an extended timeline from when the &quot;final&quot; PDFs were released to backers, and the relevant dates/OPP comments/actions since as those pertain to the release too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12986-jargogle-bamboozle","name":"Jargogle Bamboozle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T11:01:37-07:00","id":1304644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jargogle Bamboozle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1304470-timeline-of-the-scion-ks-printing?p=1304585#post1304585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for this. Do you have an extended timeline from when the &amp;quot;final&amp;quot; PDFs were released to backers, and the relevant dates/OPP comments/actions since as those pertain to the release too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I didn\u2019t initially because those events were only a few days before this post, but I added them for completeness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}